     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Thanks Ben!<br><br>I got it working with a few tweaks. The ids have to be passed to stan from R after making them ordinal. I just did as.numeric(as.factor(ids)).</div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><br><br>On Tuesday, July 21, 2015 at 7:41:45 PM UTC-4, Ben Goodrich wrote:<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">There are a variety of ways to do it. The one that is closest to your current code is to pass integer arrays of length NT to the data block called country_id and year_id. Then if you loop over the data country_id[i] returns the country index for the i-th individual and year_id[i] returns the year index for the i-th individual. If you embed those as parameter indices, like alpha[country_id[i]] and gamma[year_id[i]], you can extract from vectors whose lengths are N and T respectively.<br><br>Ben<br><br>On Tuesday, July 21, 2015 at 3:52:25 PM UTC-4, Richard McAlexander wrote:<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">I have successfuly run a stan model using unbalanced panel data (organied by country-year) with varying intercepts for each country. However, I would also like to try and include time fixed-effects (or model it hiearchically). <br><br>I can do one or the other by sorting my data frame in R, using dplyr and the summarise/group_by function to count the number of rows for each country, taking the cumulative sum of that, and then passing that vector to my stan model by looping over the vector of cumulative sums. This works great. <br><br>However I am at a loss as to how to do this for both time and country effects simulatenously, largely because I can only sort my data by either country or year. Any suggestions?<br><br>Thanks,<br>-Rick<br><br>For reference, here&#39;s the relevant part of how I am doing the country effects:<br><br><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#800\">#first get the number of rows for each country</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>countrycounts</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\">summarise</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">group_by</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">my_df</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\">country</span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span style=\"color:#000\">n</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\">n</span><span style=\"color:#660\">())</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\">#before I pass it to stan I have to format and subtract off the last entry</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>numbers</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#008\">as</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">integer</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">unlist</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">cumsum</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">countrycounts$n</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)))+</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>numbers</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">length</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">numbers</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)]&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\">numbers</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">length</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">numbers</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)]-</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\">#I pass this to my stan model in Rstan, and also pass J as an interger indicating the number of countries</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\">#relevant stan model code:</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br>model</span><span style=\"color:#660\">{</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#008\">int</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> row_mark</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> row_mark</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br>  </span><span style=\"color:#008\">for</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">l </span><span style=\"color:#008\">in</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#000\">numbers</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]){</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><span style=\"color:#000\">y</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">l</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">~</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> normal</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">intercept</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> X</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">l</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]*</span><span style=\"color:#000\">beta</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\">sigma</span><span style=\"color:#660\">);</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span></div><span style=\"color:#000\">  </span><span style=\"color:#660\">}</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br>  </span><span style=\"color:#008\">for</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">j <